<title>HUNGARY: Hungary Creditanstalt to launch two open-end funds.</title>
<headline>Hungary Creditanstalt to launch two open-end funds.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's Creditanstalt Securities will launch open-ended bond and stock investment funds on January 13 with an initial offering of 100 million forints each, the company said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Name: CA Kotveny Alap (bond fund)</p>
<p>Series A - bearer</p>
<p>Series B - registered</p>
<p>Nominal value: 1 Hungarian forint/unit</p>
<p>Subscription price: nominal value</p>
<p>Minimum subscription: 100,000 Hungarian forints</p>
<p>Subscription period: January 13 to 17</p>
<p>Name: CA Reszveny Alap (stock fund)</p>
<p>Series A - bearer</p>
<p>Series B - registered</p>
<p>Nominal value: 1 Hungarian forint/unit</p>
<p>Subscription price: nominal value</p>
<p>Minimum subscription: 100,000 Hungarian forints</p>
<p>Subscription period: January 13 to 17</p>
<p>In both funds, Series A is available for domestic and Series B for foreign investors. Series B nominal value is limited to 20 percent of the total fund capital or a maximum three billion forints.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
</text>
